+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** `request_helpers.client_ip` / `client_user_agent` slice by **graphemes** (Gleam `string.slice`) while the DB CHECK bounds count **characters** (Postgres `length()`) — a multi-codepoint header (emoji ZWJ sequences, combining marks, flags) can exceed the bound post-slice and 500 the write path.
+
+**Approach:** Replace grapheme-based slicing with **codepoint-bounded** slicing in the two helper functions. The helpers feed `cookie_consent_log`, `payment_terms_acceptance`, and `application.submitted_*` — all share the same 64/512 CHECK idiom, so the fix lands in one focused change in `request_helpers.gleam` and applies to all three callers unchanged.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Never split a multi-byte character (codepoint-boundary slicing only).
+- Result must never exceed the DB CHECK character bounds: 64 for IP, 512 for UA — for ANY input, including adversarial multi-codepoint headers.
+- One focused change in `request_helpers.gleam`; the three callers (`consent_handler`, `payment_handler`, `application_handler`) need no edits.
+- Regression test with a multi-codepoint header that previously would exceed the bound post-slice, proving the write path no longer 500s.
+- Existing suites green: `make test-server` / `make test-shared` (client untouched).
+
+**Ask First:** (none — deferred-work item pre-approved via briefing)
+
+**Never:**
+- No unrelated refactors, no notification work (RC4.4 owns that).
+- No changes to the SQL CHECK constraints or migrations.
+- No behavior change for single-codepoint-per-grapheme input (ASCII/typical UAs must truncate exactly as before: 64/512 chars).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| ASCII over-long UA | 600× "U" | exactly 512 chars stored | N/A |
+| ASCII over-long XFF | 500× "9" first hop | exactly 64 chars stored | N/A |
+| Emoji ZWJ-heavy UA (multi-codepoint graphemes) | e.g. repeated family emoji, ≥512 codepoints in first 512 graphemes | stored value ≤512 characters (codepoints); no 500 | never trips CHECK |
+| Emoji/multi-codepoint XFF garbage | ≥64 codepoints in first 64 graphemes | stored value ≤64 characters; no 500 | never trips CHECK |
+| Header absent | no `x-forwarded-for` / `user-agent` | `''` stored; submission unaffected | N/A |
+| XFF with comma list | `"a,b,c"` | first entry only, trimmed, bounded | N/A |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
