+## Spec Change Log
+
+## Design Notes
+
+Gleam `string.slice` operates on **grapheme clusters** (e.g. 👨👩👧👦 = 1 grapheme, 7 codepoints; combining sequences similar). Postgres `length(text)` counts **characters = codepoints**. So 512 graphemes of ZWJ emoji can be ~3,584 codepoints — the CHECK `length(user_agent) <= 512` rejects the row → 500 on the application write path (payment/consent handlers catch insert errors, but the application transaction aborts).
+
+Fix: `string.to_utf_codepoints |> list.take(max) |> string.from_utf_codepoints` — codepoint-boundary slicing is atomic (never splits a multi-byte char), and the output has ≤ `max` codepoints, so Postgres `length()` can never exceed the CHECK. ASCII/typical UAs are 1 codepoint per grapheme → identical truncation to today.
+
